# Copy to desk/.env.local (gitignored) and fill in only what you need.
# Every line is optional. With none of them set, the desk runs on the Claude CLI for text,
# Ollama for photo reads and lesson search, and the browser's own voice.

# Photo reads (Math Buddy's camera). Easiest: the Claude CLI you already signed in to, no Ollama.
# Values: ollama (the default), claude-cli, codex.
DESK_VISION_ENGINE=claude-cli
# CLAUDE_VISION_MODEL=sonnet

# Text engine: the Claude Code CLI, headless (claude -p). Needs `claude` on PATH and signed in.
# CLAUDE_BIN=claude
# CLAUDE_FAST_MODEL=haiku
# CLAUDE_BEST_MODEL=sonnet

# Ollama (photo reads when DESK_VISION_ENGINE=ollama, and lesson search embeddings).
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b
# OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# Where the desk keeps learners, sessions and the TV key. Default: desk/data/
# DESK_DATA_DIR=

# The TV's voice. Without these, the TV uses the browser's speech.
# PIPER_BIN=
# PIPER_VOICE=
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=

# Speech to text server (optional; the phone also listens in the browser).
# STT_URL=http://localhost:8080
# STT_API_KEY=
